      <title>0MQ: Multithreading magic</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Lightning Talks</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Multi-core boxes are becoming mainstream, but software tools are not keeping with the hardware evolution. Classic multithreading programming is complex and error-prone. Systematic solutions, like Erlang programming language, on the other hand are limited to small niches and are hard to use in real-world legacy environments. The talk explains how 0MQ can be used to bring Erlang-style message-based concurrency to any language in literally couple of minutes.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
